      "source": [
        "import polars as pl\n",
        "import requests #new for reading in JSON\n",
        "import io       #new for reading in JSON\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "from lets_plot import *\n",
        "\n",
        "LetsPlot.setup_html(isolated_frame=True)"
      ],
      "id": "37f5a759",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Learn morea about Code Cells: https://quarto.org/docs/reference/cells/cells-jupyter.html\n",
        "\n",
        "# Include and execute your code here\n",
        "url = \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/byuidatascience/data4missing/master/data-raw/flights_missing/flights_missing.json\"\n",
        "response = requests.get(url)\n",
        "df = pl.read_json(io.BytesIO(response.content))\n",
        "df.head()"
      ],
      "id": "1787b864",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## QUESTION 1\n",
        "\n",
        "__Calculate the sample size (i.e. number of rows in the dataset) for each airport in each year__. What do you notice?\n",
        "\n",
        "I noticed that there are 89 combinations of airport and years, being 8 different airports and 12 different years. In addition, there is one airport the name was not reported and that has less months reported than it should have.\n",
        "\n",
        "_AI use reflection_\n",
        "**Link** to the original chat:\n",
        "**The Process** How exactly did you use the tool?\n",
        "**The Impact**  How did using AI impact your learning?"
      ],
      "id": "350ce890"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Include and execute your code here\n",
        "sample_size = df.group_by(['airport_name', 'year']).agg(pl.len().alias('Sample Size')).sort(['airport_name', 'year'])\n",
        "\n",
        "print(sample_size)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(df.select(pl.col('airport_name').n_unique()))\n",
        "\n",
        "print(df.select(pl.col('year').n_unique()))\n"
      ],
      "id": "72fdb512",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## QUESTION 2\n",
        "\n",
        "__Which airport has the worst delays?__ Describe the metric you chose, and why you chose it to determine the “worst” airport. Your answer should include a summary table that lists (for each airport) the total number of flights, total number of delayed flights, proportion of delayed flights, and average delay time in hours. \n",
        "\n",
        "I decided that the worst airport is the one that has the highest proportion of delayed flights because it measures the ineficiency of that airport. Using that metric, the San Francisco airport is considered the worst airport.\n",
        "\n",
        "would be the one that has the highest proportion of delayed flights\n",
        "San Diego airport has the highest proportion of delayed flights.\n",
        "\n",
        "_AI use reflection_\n",
        "**Link** to the original chat:\n",
        "**The Process** How exactly did you use the tool?\n",
        "**The Impact**  How did using AI impact your learning?"
      ],
      "id": "0b53f281"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Include and execute your code here\n",
        "# pior eh o que tem mais atrasos e mais longos?\n",
        "# TOTAL NUMBER OF FLIGHTS = num_of_delays_total\n",
        "\n",
        "#\n",
        "\n",
        "worse_airport = df.group_by('airport_name').agg(pl.col('num_of_flights_total').sum().alias('Total Flights'), \n",
        "# print(airports)\n",
        "\n",
        "pl.col('num_of_delays_total').sum().alias('Total Delayed Flights'), \n",
        "\n",
        "(pl.col('num_of_delays_total').sum() / pl.col('num_of_flights_total').sum()).alias('Proportion of Delayed flights'),\n",
        "\n",
        "((pl.col('minutes_delayed_total').sum() / 60) / pl.col('num_of_delays_total').sum()).alias('Average Delay Time in Hours')).sort('Proportion of Delayed flights', descending=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "print(worse_airport)\n"
      ],
      "id": "452ec9c5",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## QUESTION 3\n",
        "\n",
        "__Create a barplot showing the proportion of all flights that are delayed at each airport. Describe what you learn from this graph.__  \n",
        "\n",
        "From this graph I was able to learn that 4 of the airports having similar proportions of delayed flights and that Sale Lake City is has the smallest number of delayed flights\n",
        "\n",
        "_AI use reflection_\n",
        "**Link** to the original chat:\n",
        "**The Process** How exactly did you use the tool?\n",
        "**The Impact**  How did using AI impact your learning?"
      ],
      "id": "631a9488"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "df_plot = worse_airport.to_pandas()\n",
        "\n",
        "# 2. Cria o gráfico direto de uma vez só!\n",
        "df_plot.plot.bar(\n",
        "    x='airport_name', \n",
        "    y='Proportion of Delayed flights', \n",
        "    title='Proportion of Delayed Flights by Airport',\n",
        "    figsize=(12, 6)\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "2d23d878",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    }
